<!-- The status-bar / shade icon: the wordmark's own "TC" monogram, taken as
     curves from the brand master (`assets/logo/tailchat-light-outlined.svg`,
     JetBrains Mono Bold outlines) and scaled into 24dp.

     It used to be the brand cat's ears-and-head silhouette with the eyes as
     cutouts, and the owner reported what that came to at status-bar size: an
     angry cat, not a logo. There is no room there for the tile, the whiskers or
     the cat's face, and the two surviving features — sharp ears above two round
     eyes — are exactly the ones that read as a scowl. The lettering is the
     other half of the same mark, it is what the app is *called*, and two
     letters with real counters survive tinting to one flat colour at 24dp
     better than any facial feature does.

     Letters only, no panel: the system tints the whole icon to a single colour
     and draws it over whatever the bar is showing, so a background would be
     flattened into the glyph anyway. -->
